{
  "module": "Output side: from scores to text",
  "lesson": {
    "slug": "temperature-decoding",
    "title": "Temperature, top-k and top-p",
    "summary": "How the choice of next token can be steered: temperature reshapes the distribution, and greedy, top-k and top-p decide which tokens can be picked.",
    "covers": ["temperature", "decoding-strategies"],
    "prerequisites": [
      {
        "lesson": "logits-softmax",
        "reason": "Temperature divides the logits before softmax, so both must already be understood."
      },
      {
        "lesson": "next-token-sampling",
        "reason": "Greedy, top-k and top-p are ways of choosing the sample from the next-token distribution."
      }
    ]
  },
  "screens": [
    {
      "ref": "knobs",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Sampling is not one fixed rule. Some settings let you steer how adventurous or how safe the chosen token is."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Four ideas cover most of what you will meet: "
            },
            {
              "text": "temperature",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": ", "
            },
            {
              "text": "greedy",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": ", "
            },
            {
              "text": "top-k",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": " and "
            },
            {
              "text": "top-p",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": ". Temperature reshapes the distribution before a token is chosen. The other three are rules for choosing."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "sources": [
        {
          "title": "Transformers in LLMs: mechanics and pipeline (flashkarte deck, cards 15, 70, 71)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "ref": "temperature",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Temperature",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": ", written T, is a number that divides the logits before softmax:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "formula",
          "latex": "\\mathrm{softmax}(z / T)",
          "spoken": "softmax of z divided by T"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "With "
            },
            {
              "text": "T = 1",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": " nothing changes: you get the model's own distribution. Any other T reshapes it."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "sources": [
        {
          "title": "Transformers in LLMs: mechanics and pipeline (flashkarte deck, cards 70)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "ref": "low-temperature",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "A "
            },
            {
              "text": "temperature below 1",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": " makes the distribution "
            },
            {
              "text": "sharper",
              "italic": true
            },
            {
              "text": ". On the toy logits 3, 2, 1, -1:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            [
              {
                "text": "T = 1: 0.657, 0.242, 0.089, 0.012"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "text": "T = 0.5: 0.867, 0.117, 0.016, 0.000"
              }
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "The likely token becomes even more likely and the others fade. As T approaches 0 the distribution collapses onto the top token, which is exactly "
            },
            {
              "text": "greedy",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": " choice."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "sources": [
        {
          "title": "Transformers in LLMs: mechanics and pipeline (flashkarte deck, cards 70)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "ref": "high-temperature",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "A "
            },
            {
              "text": "temperature above 1",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": " makes the distribution "
            },
            {
              "text": "flatter",
              "italic": true
            },
            {
              "text": ":"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            [
              {
                "text": "T = 1: 0.657, 0.242, 0.089, 0.012"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "text": "T = 2: 0.474, 0.287, 0.174, 0.064"
              }
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Now unlikely tokens get a bigger share. The samples become more diverse, and also more random."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "tone": "note",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Temperature changes the probabilities. It does not remove any token from the vocabulary."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "sources": [
        {
          "title": "Transformers in LLMs: mechanics and pipeline (flashkarte deck, cards 70)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "ref": "top-k",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Top-k",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": " sampling cuts off the tail. Keep only the "
            },
            {
              "text": "k",
              "italic": true
            },
            {
              "text": " most probable tokens, "
            },
            {
              "text": "renormalise",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": " so they add up to 1 again, and then sample from those."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "On the toy distribution with k = 2, keep "
            },
            {
              "text": "mat",
              "italic": true
            },
            {
              "text": " and "
            },
            {
              "text": "sofa",
              "italic": true
            },
            {
              "text": ". Together they hold 0.899, so dividing by that gives 0.731, 0.269. "
            },
            {
              "text": "floor",
              "italic": true
            },
            {
              "text": " and "
            },
            {
              "text": "moon",
              "italic": true
            },
            {
              "text": " can no longer be picked."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Greedy is the extreme case of k = 1."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "sources": [
        {
          "title": "Transformers in LLMs: mechanics and pipeline (flashkarte deck, cards 71)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "ref": "top-p",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Top-p",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": ", also called "
            },
            {
              "text": "nucleus",
              "italic": true
            },
            {
              "text": " sampling, keeps the smallest set of tokens whose probabilities add up to at least "
            },
            {
              "text": "p",
              "italic": true
            },
            {
              "text": ", renormalises, and samples."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "With p = 0.9 on the toy distribution: "
            },
            {
              "text": "mat",
              "italic": true
            },
            {
              "text": " alone gives 0.657, "
            },
            {
              "text": "mat",
              "italic": true
            },
            {
              "text": " and "
            },
            {
              "text": "sofa",
              "italic": true
            },
            {
              "text": " give 0.899, still below 0.9, and with "
            },
            {
              "text": "floor",
              "italic": true
            },
            {
              "text": " the total reaches 0.988. So three tokens are kept, with renormalised probabilities 0.665, 0.245, 0.090."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "The size of the kept set "
            },
            {
              "text": "adapts",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": ". If the model is very sure and one token holds 0.95, that token alone is enough. If it is unsure, many tokens are kept. Top-k always keeps exactly k."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "sources": [
        {
          "title": "Transformers in LLMs: mechanics and pipeline (flashkarte deck, cards 71)"
        },
        {
          "title": "Holtzman et al. 2019, The Curious Case of Neural Text Degeneration",
          "url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/1904.09751"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "ref": "combining",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "These are different kinds of change. Temperature "
            },
            {
              "text": "reshapes",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": " the whole distribution. Top-k and top-p "
            },
            {
              "text": "restrict",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": " which tokens are allowed. Greedy skips the randomness altogether."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "They can be used together: for example, set a temperature first, and then apply top-p to the reshaped distribution."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "sources": [
        {
          "title": "Transformers in LLMs: mechanics and pipeline (flashkarte deck, cards 15, 70, 71)"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "questions": [
